  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: db176a60e3b58b4408636b22a97519c4, type: 3}
  m_Name: OxygenSystemFailureEvent
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MarsEvent
  eventTitle: Oxygen System Failure
  eventDescription: Warning! The Mars outpost's oxygen generation system has malfunctioned,
    causing oxygen reserves to decrease. The crew depends on a stable oxygen supply
    to survive. You must decide how to restore the system while managing the base's
    limited resources.
  targetSol: 4
  optionATitle: Repair Oxygen Generator
  energyChangeA: -12
  lifeSupportChangeA: 18
  shieldChangeA: 0
  resultTitleA: Oxygen Generator Repaired
  resultDescriptionA: The crew successfully repairs the oxygen generation system.
    Oxygen production returns to normal, improving life support conditions inside
    the habitat. However, the repair operation consumes a significant amount of energy.
  optionBTitle: Activate Backup Oxygen System
  energyChangeB: -5
  lifeSupportChangeB: 8
  shieldChangeB: -5
  resultTitleB: Backup Oxygen System Activated
  resultDescriptionB: The backup oxygen system is activated successfully, stabilizing
    the crew's oxygen supply. This temporary solution requires less energy than a
    full repair, but redirects resources away from radiation protection, reducing
    shield integrity.
  educationalExplanation: Astronauts depend on life support systems to maintain breathable
    air inside spacecraft and space habitats. NASA uses oxygen generation and air
    revitalization technologies to support long-duration missions. Reliable oxygen
    production, carbon dioxide removal, and backup systems are essential for keeping
    astronauts safe during space exploration.
  scientificSource: "NASA \u2014 Environmental Control and Life Support System"
  scientificSourceURL: https://www.nasa.gov/reference/environmental-control-and-life-support-system-eclss/
